course: dictionary
lesson: 9679
title: Suction: pulling with air
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Suction is a pulling force. It happens when air or liquid is taken out of a space, so the air or liquid around it pushes in to fill the gap. That push is what pulls things in or holds them on.
explain: When you drink through a straw, you take air out of the straw with your mouth. The air outside pushes your drink up the straw and into your mouth. That pushing is suction.
explain: A vacuum cleaner works by suction: it removes air from its nozzle, so the air outside pushes dust and dirt in. Suction cups and suction pads stick to smooth surfaces in the same way, because the air under them has been pushed out.
fact: Suction is a pulling force made when air or liquid is removed from a space.
fact: Suction works because the air outside pushes in when the air inside has been taken out.
fact: Suction is an uncountable noun, so we say «strong suction», not «a suction».
fact: A «suction cup» is a cup-shaped pad that sticks to a surface by suction.
fact: Octopus arms have suckers that grip by suction, so an octopus can hold on tightly to rocks.
exercise: «Keep hair, fingers and toys away from pool drains, because strong suction can hold you under.» What is suction in this sentence? | A loud splash | A coloured tile on the pool floor | A kind of swimming stroke | *A pulling force that can hold you in place
exercise: A vacuum cleaner works by suction. What does it do? | Heats the room up | *Pulls dust and dirt in | Pushes water out of the pool | Makes the room lighter
exercise: Why do octopus suckers grip so well? | *Because air is taken out, so the air outside holds them on | Because they are very heavy | Because they are cold | Because they are sticky with glue
test: Suction is made when what is removed from a space? | Sand | *Air or liquid | Sound | Light
test: Which phrase names a cup-shaped pad that sticks to glass? | *Suction cup | Paper clip | Drinking bottle | Sponge bag
exam: Which best explains how drinking through a straw works? | Air is pushed into the straw from the top | The drink is heated so it rises up the straw | The straw pulls the drink with a magnet | *Air is taken out of the straw, so the air outside pushes the drink up
